###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - MLIPAudit reports normalised scores between 0 and 1 (overall, per category and per benchmark; Tables 2-3, 7-10), which are not energy/force errors. Dihedral-scan, conformer and reactivity MAEs/RMSEs are shown only in Figs. 2, 4 and 5 (the text gives bounds such as MAE below 0.12 kcal/mol).
# - The internal SPICE2 models are trained as in Brunken et al. (brunken2025) but are separate nodes here; UMA-Small, MACE-OFF and MACE-MP checkpoints are not named precisely.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/wehrhan2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
